1
00:00:06,770 --> 00:00:11,560
A family drives 120 kilometres to a beach in 1 and a half hours.

2
00:00:11,610 --> 00:00:17,030
They stay 2 hours, then drive home in 2 hours because of traffic.

3
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:20,050
On which part of the trip were they fastest?

4
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:23,290
Pause the video and choose.

5
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:27,270
Going out, they drove 120 kilometres in 1.5 hours.

6
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:29,740
That is 80 kilometres per hour.

7
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:34,750
Coming home took 2 hours, which is only 60 kilometres per hour.

8
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:37,770
So they were fastest going out.

9
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:41,730
Remember: speed equals distance divided by time.

10
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:45,170
On a distance-time graph, the gradient is the speed.

11
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:47,020
A steeper line means faster.

12
00:00:47,070 --> 00:00:48,740
A flat line means stopped.

13
00:00:48,790 --> 00:00:51,810
A line sloping down means coming back.

14
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:52,560
Your turn.

15
00:00:52,610 --> 00:00:57,380
What was their speed on the way home: 120 kilometres in 2 hours?

16
00:00:57,430 --> 00:01:00,820
Pause the video and try it.

17
00:01:00,870 --> 00:01:04,090
120 divided by 2 is 60 kilometres per hour.

18
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:06,900
The shape of any graph tells a story.

19
00:01:06,950 --> 00:01:09,640
A straight line means a steady rate.

20
00:01:09,690 --> 00:01:12,850
A curve means the rate is changing.

21
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:18,180
Fill a tall, thin vase with water at a steady rate, and the depth rises quickly.

22
00:01:18,230 --> 00:01:20,860
In a wide bowl, it rises slowly.

23
00:01:20,910 --> 00:01:22,170
Here is the method.

24
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:25,430
Step 1: read the title, the axes and the units.

25
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:27,080
Check the scale.

26
00:01:27,130 --> 00:01:29,170
Step 2: describe each section.

27
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:31,610
Is it going up, flat or going down?

28
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:33,270
Steep or gentle?

29
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:39,470
Step 3: work out rates as gradients, like speed equals distance divided by time.

30
00:01:39,520 --> 00:01:43,790
Step 4: explain what it means in the real situation.

31
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:48,370
Find the average speed for the whole trip, including the stop.

32
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:51,110
The total distance is 240 kilometres.

33
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:54,390
The total time is 5 and a half hours.

34
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:58,890
240 divided by 5.5 is about 43.6 kilometres per hour.

35
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:02,240
The stop brings the average down.

36
00:02:02,290 --> 00:02:06,840
Water flows steadily into a cylinder with a narrowing funnel on top.

37
00:02:06,890 --> 00:02:12,990
In the cylinder, the depth rises at a steady rate, so the graph is a straight line.

38
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:18,250
In the funnel, the space gets narrower, so the depth rises faster and faster.

39
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:21,670
The graph curves upwards, getting steeper.

40
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:22,370
Your turn.

41
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:25,650
A curve getting steeper means the rate is what?

42
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:28,230
Pause and choose.

43
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:31,750
Getting steeper means the rate is increasing.

44
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:38,560
And if two people's lines cross on a distance-time graph, they are at the same place at the same time.

45
00:02:38,610 --> 00:02:39,780
They meet.

46
00:02:39,830 --> 00:02:43,840
A distance-time graph reaches 60 kilometres at 2 hours.

47
00:02:43,890 --> 00:02:45,390
Zara finds the speed.

48
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:48,000
Which line goes wrong first?

49
00:02:48,050 --> 00:02:49,140
Line 2 is wrong.

50
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:52,320
The height shows the distance, not the speed.

51
00:02:52,370 --> 00:02:54,710
The speed is the gradient.

52
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:59,000
60 divided by 2 is 30 kilometres per hour.

53
00:02:59,050 --> 00:03:02,680
A running app draws a distance-time graph of your run.

54
00:03:02,730 --> 00:03:05,140
Steep parts show where you ran fast.

55
00:03:05,190 --> 00:03:09,780
Flat parts show where you stopped, maybe at a traffic light.

56
00:03:09,830 --> 00:03:14,870
The app's pace is just the gradient of the graph, worked out for you.

57
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:16,180
One last question.

58
00:03:16,230 --> 00:03:20,480
9 kilometres in 45 minutes is how many kilometres per hour?

59
00:03:20,530 --> 00:03:23,850
Pause the video and answer.

60
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:27,350
45 minutes is three quarters of an hour.

61
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,440
9 divided by 0.75 is 12.

62
00:03:29,490 --> 00:03:35,060
Or: 3 kilometres every 15 minutes, which is 12 in an hour.

63
00:03:35,110 --> 00:03:39,610
To remember: on a distance-time graph, the gradient is the speed.

64
00:03:39,660 --> 00:03:40,940
Flat means stopped.

65
00:03:40,990 --> 00:03:43,100
Down means coming back.

66
00:03:43,150 --> 00:03:45,530
A straight line means a steady rate.

67
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:48,110
A curve means a changing rate.

68
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:52,460
Average speed is total distance divided by total time.

69
00:03:52,510 --> 00:03:55,290
Describe each section in context.

70
00:03:55,340 --> 00:04:00,710
Great work! Now practise lesson 11.4 on Camday.
